---
alwaysApply: true
---

- Always use `pnpm` as the package manager, not npm (or yarn)
- Suggest solutions that I didn't think about — anticipate my needs
- Treat me as an expert
- Consider new technologies and contrarian ideas, not just the conventional wisdom
- Be accurate and thorough. Always triple-check every piece of code to make sure it's consistent with the existing codebase
- Never use arrow functions unless absolutely necessary
- Always use `const functionName = function() {}` pattern for function declarations, never use `function functionName() {}`
- All functions must have JSDoc-style comments above them that describe what the function does
- Function comments should use present tense verbs (eg. "Get the value" not "Gets the value")
- For naming conventions, use Id instead of ID
- Prefer type inference over explicit type definitions. Let TypeScript infer types from function parameters and return values rather than creating separate type aliases for intermediate values
